            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0247" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23814: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Salina
                        Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burlingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-05T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1920—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 3, 9 A.M.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d158-f1"/></p>
                <p>Navy Department is despatching additional vessels to Mexican east coast, and war
                    ships will call at intervals at Gulf ports, including Puerto Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
